WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:01.376
- I don't like it.

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:03.587
- Try again.

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:06.965
I need to know why
you don't like it.

00:00:10.469 --> 00:00:13.555
- The food is really important.
We really decided to do it

00:00:13.639 --> 00:00:17.351
as a metaphor for what is
going on in each episode,

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:20.437
and also what the main characters
are feeling, and especially Sean.

00:00:20.521 --> 00:00:22.606
- I mean, I literally
can't taste it.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:24.983
- Okay, now you're being rude.
And we have guests.

00:00:26.902 --> 00:00:30.155
- Food has to feed emotionally
into the characters,

00:00:30.239 --> 00:00:32.866
and thematically
into the episode.

00:00:33.742 --> 00:00:36.453
- He advises for some of
the best restaurants in the city.

00:00:36.537 --> 00:00:39.623
- I, uh, feed butter and cream
to fat people.

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:43.168
- Sean is the kind of chef
that like to challenge you.

00:00:45.921 --> 00:00:48.423
So whatever he finds,
he wants to cook.

00:00:48.507 --> 00:00:49.550
- Strawberry?

00:00:50.384 --> 00:00:52.427
- Lobster.

00:00:52.511 --> 00:00:53.720
(spoon clatters)

00:00:53.804 --> 00:00:55.514
- Julian.

00:00:55.597 --> 00:00:57.641
- The foods a huge part,

00:00:57.724 --> 00:01:00.435
and we're taking what
Anthony Basgallop has written,

00:01:00.519 --> 00:01:03.814
and making sure that it's usable.
So it's nice.

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:05.607
It's a lot of life imitating art,

00:01:05.691 --> 00:01:08.652
and a lot of very giving people
who are willing to learn

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:11.321
and willing to impart their knowledge
and what they've learned.

00:01:11.989 --> 00:01:14.575
- Marc Vetri is one of
the great chefs in the world,

00:01:14.658 --> 00:01:18.161
so we asked him would he want to
be the consultant on the show.

00:01:18.245 --> 00:01:20.706
And we're so lucky to have him

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:23.542
and Chef Drew here
to be on set every day,

00:01:23.625 --> 00:01:25.460
setting everything up,
you know, designing it,

00:01:25.544 --> 00:01:27.421
talking us through everything.

00:01:27.504 --> 00:01:31.425
Also, Toby, who plays Sean,
loves to cook. He's all in.

00:01:31.508 --> 00:01:32.843
They're in the kitchen on the set,

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:35.012
which is a real kitchen,
and they're cooking stuff,

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:38.432
and so it makes it feel real
in every way because it is real.

00:01:38.515 --> 00:01:40.934
- No, don't. I mean, she likes
the idea of spicy food,

00:01:41.018 --> 00:01:43.979
but in reality,
it doesn't agree with her, so...

00:01:44.855 --> 00:01:47.524
As long as she believes it's there,
she swears she can taste it.

00:01:49.985 --> 00:01:52.362
- Really, when you get into food,
and you talk to a lot of chefs,

00:01:52.446 --> 00:01:54.364
and you're dealing with that,
they see it as life-giving.

00:01:54.448 --> 00:01:57.034
That's how it's been threaded
through the show.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:02:00.579
That the food, yes,
is extravagant and over the top,

00:02:00.662 --> 00:02:02.456
and kind of
a little overbearing,

00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:05.375
but in the end, really,
is life-giving.

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:07.961
- The trout is delicious.

00:02:08.045 --> 00:02:12.257
- I love precision of food, and I do find
the great chefs super-inspiring to me.

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:16.261
I'm inspired by how they're driven,
the precision of it,

00:02:16.345 --> 00:02:17.888
the discipline involved and the craft.

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:20.349
I try to bring that here.

